  "description": "layout center puts a cell narrower than its column in the middle of it rather than at its start. Six cells of six different widths in a three-column grid: every cell but the widest of each column is nudged by half its column's slack. Three more grids, each for a rule that only shows when it is asked for and refused. The second asks to be centred and states no `align`: upstream's centring step reads the flag its alignment branch sets \u2014 `if (alignCol && get(opt.center, Column) && nrows > 1)` \u2014 and the branch an unstated `align` takes begins by clearing it, so nothing moves. The third states `columns: 0`, which is `ncols = opt.columns || groups.length` and puts all six in one row rather than one column. The fourth is `bounds: \"flush\"` over cells that declare no size: `bboxFlush` is `(0, 0, item.width || 0, item.height || 0)` with no fallback, so each measures as nothing and the grid collapses to its own padding.",
